# Creating a witness for each person
#
# Socrates and Plato are both humans. An N3 rule introduces a fresh blank-
# node witness for each rule application, showing an existential variable
# in a rule conclusion.

@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix : <http://example.org/socrates#> .

# Facts: two humans.
:Socrates a :Human .
:Plato a :Human .

# Every human is something: the blank node _:B in the conclusion is
# existential, so each firing introduces a fresh individual.
{
    ?S a :Human .
} => {
    ?S :is _:B .
} .
